  </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────── Numbers ───────────── -->
<section class="sec stats">
  <div class="wrap stats-in">
    <div class="stat" data-up><b data-count="12">12</b><span>modules, take only what you need</span></div>
    <div class="stat" data-up><b data-count="1">1</b><span>login for office, teachers and principal</span></div>
    <div class="stat" data-up><b data-count="0">0</b><span>rows typed again from your Excel</span></div>
    <div class="stat" data-up><b data-count="4">4</b><span>steps from demo to go-live</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────── Modules ───────────── -->
<section class="sec" id="modules">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head" data-up>
      <span class="kicker">Modules</span>
      <h2>Everything a school runs on, <span class="grad">in one place</span></h2>
      <p>Switch a module on when you are ready for it. One you do not use never gets in the way.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mods">
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c1"><i class="bx bx-user-plus"></i></span><h3>Admissions</h3><p>Enquiry, follow-ups, registration and admission in one flow. Admission form, documents, ID cards.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c2"><i class="bx bx-wallet"></i></span><h3>Fees &amp; receipts</h3><p>Fee structure per class, collect at the counter, instant receipts, concessions, month-wise dues, day close.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c3"><i class="bx bx-calendar-check"></i></span><h3>Attendance</h3><p>Class teachers mark in seconds on the phone. Absent students' parents get a WhatsApp alert.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c4"><i class="bx bx-medal"></i></span><h3>Exams &amp; results</h3><p>Datesheet, admit cards, marks entry by subject teacher, grades, ranks and printable report cards.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c5"><i class="bx bx-time-five"></i></span><h3>Timetable &amp; homework</h3><p>Clash-free timetable, substitutes for absent teachers, the school bell, and homework with who-did-it.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c6"><i class="bx bx-group"></i></span><h3>Staff &amp; salary</h3><p>Staff records, staff attendance, leave, monthly salary and payslips that staff can open themselves.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c7"><i class="bx bx-bus"></i></span><h3>Transport</h3><p>Routes, stops, vehicles and riders, with transport fee added to the child's fees automatically.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c8"><i class="bx bx-package"></i></span><h3>School store</h3><p>Books, uniform and stationery: purchase, stock, issue to students and sale with receipts.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c9"><i class="bx bx-line-chart"></i></span><h3>Accounts</h3><p>Expenses by category and a cash book, next to your fee collection, so the day's money adds up.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c10"><i class="bx bx-certification"></i></span><h3>Certificates &amp; TC</h3><p>Transfer certificates, bonafide and character certificates printed with the school's seal and signature.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c11"><i class="bx bx-bell"></i></span><h3>Notices &amp; calendar</h3><p>Notice board for staff and parents, holidays and events on the school calendar.</p></article>
      <article class="mod tilt"><span class="mi c12"><i class="bx bx-lock-alt"></i></span><h3>Roles &amp; permissions</h3><p>Principal, accountant, teacher, front desk: each sees only what their job needs.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────── Why us ───────────── -->
<section class="sec why-sec" id="why">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="kicker">Why SmartSchoolWala</span>
    @* home.js lights this up word by word as it scrolls past *@
    <p class="big-say" id="bigSay">We sat with school offices before writing a line: how fees are collected at the counter, how a class teacher marks attendance between periods, how results go out. The software follows that, so your staff do not have to change how they work.</p>
    <div class="why-grid">
      <div class="why-card tilt" data-up><i class="bx bx-mobile-alt"></i><h3>Phone first</h3><p>Teachers mark attendance and enter marks from their phone. Install it on the home screen like an app.</p></div>
      <div class="why-card tilt" data-up><i class="bx bxl-whatsapp"></i><h3>Parents stay informed</h3><p>Absent alerts, fee reminders and notices reach parents on WhatsApp.</p></div>
      <div class="why-card tilt" data-up><i class="bx bx-shield-quarter"></i><h3>Safe and private</h3><p>Each school's data is kept apart, student photos open only for your staff, and every role sees only its part.</p></div>
      <div class="why-card tilt" data-up><i class="bx bx-receipt"></i><h3>Money that adds up</h3><p>Every receipt is numbered, cancellations need a reason, and the day close shows what each counter collected.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────── Getting started ───────────── -->
<section class="sec" id="switch">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head" data-up>
      <span class="kicker">Getting started</span>
      <h2>From your registers to live <span class="grad">in days, not months</span></h2>
      <p>No need to type in every student again. We bring your existing data over and stay with you until your office is comfortable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps-wrap">
      <div class="steps-line"><i id="stepsFill"></i></div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li data-up><span>1</span><h3>Free demo</h3><p>We show you the system with a sample school, on a call or at your school.</p></li>
        <li data-up><span>2</span><h3>Your data comes in</h3><p>Students, staff and old dues are imported from Excel and checked row by row.</p></li>
        <li data-up><span>3</span><h3>Setup &amp; training</h3><p>Classes, fee structure and timetable set up together; your staff are trained.</p></li>
        <li data-up><span>4</span><h3>Go live</h3><p>Start collecting fees and marking attendance. We are a call away when you need us.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────── FAQ ───────────── -->
<section class="sec" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap faq-wrap">
    <div class="sec-head left" data-up>
      <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
      <h2>Questions schools ask us</h2>
      <p>Anything else? Ask us on the demo call.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details data-up><summary>How much does it cost?<i class="bx bx-plus"></i></summary><p>The price depends on the number of students and the modules your school takes. Book a free demo and we will send you a quote for your school.</p></details>
      <details data-up><summary>Do we need to install anything?<i class="bx bx-plus"></i></summary><p>No. It opens in the browser on any computer or phone. On a phone you can add it to the home screen and use it like an app.</p></details>
      <details data-up><summary>We already have our data in Excel. Do we type it again?<i class="bx bx-plus"></i></summary><p>No. Students, staff and previous dues are imported from Excel. Every row is checked first, and nothing is saved until you confirm.</p></details>
      <details data-up><summary>Can a teacher see fees or salaries?<i class="bx bx-plus"></i></summary><p>Only if you allow it. Every role has its own permissions: a teacher sees their classes, the accountant sees fees, and salary stays with whoever you choose.</p></details>
      <details data-up><summary>Is our data safe?<i class="bx bx-plus"></i></summary><p>Each school's data is kept separate from every other school's. Sign-in is by password, photos and documents open only for your signed-in staff, and every receipt records who collected it.</p></details>
      <details data-up><summary>Can we start with only fees and add the rest later?<i class="bx bx-plus"></i></summary><p>Yes. Modules are switched on per school, so you can begin with what you need most and add others whenever you are ready.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ───────────── Call to action + contact ───────────── -->
<section class="sec" id="contact">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta tilt" data-up>
      <div class="cta-ring"></div>
      <div class="cta-text">
        <h2>See SmartSchoolWala on a free demo</h2>
        <p>Tell us your school's name and city. We will set up a time that suits your office.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-btns">
        <a href="@demoLink" class="btn btn-white btn-lg magnet" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><i class="bx @(WhatsApp.Length > 0 ? "bxl-whatsapp" : "bx-envelope")"></i>Book a free demo</a>
        <a href="@loginUrl" class="btn btn-outline-w btn-lg">Already a customer? Login</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="contact">
      <div data-up><span class="ci"><i class="bx bx-phone"></i></span><span><small>Call or WhatsApp</small>@PhoneShown</span></div>
      <div data-up><span class="ci"><i class="bx bx-envelope"></i></span><span><small>E-mail</small><a href="mailto:@Email">@Email</a></span></div>
      <div data-up><span class="ci"><i class="bx bx-lock-alt"></i></span><span><small>School portal</small><a href="@loginUrl">Login to your school</a></span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer class="foot">
  <div class="foot-word" aria-hidden="true">SmartSchoolWala</div>
  <div class="wrap foot-in">
    <span class="nav-logo"><img src="~/img/brand/ssw-icon.svg" alt="" /><span>SmartSchool<b>Wala</b></span></span>
    <span>© @year SmartSchoolWala.com · School ERP for Indian schools</span>
    <a href="@loginUrl">Login</a>
  </div>
</footer>

@* Three.js draws the hero desk, GSAP runs the other scroll animations. If either fails to load
   the page still shows everything: home.js only hides things it is about to animate. *@
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js"></script>
